  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n   This strategy proposes a hybrid optimization approach combining a genetic algorithm (GA) with a local search using the Nelder-Mead method. The GA provides global exploration, while the Nelder-Mead offers exploitation, ensuring better local minima discovery. The key innovation is dynamically switching from GA to Nelder-Mead when stagnation is detected in the GA, thus combining strengths of both methods to potentially find a better minimum for C\u2085.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n   - Variables: Discrete h \u2208 [0,1]^(n_points), \u2211h = n_points/2.  \n   - Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k [ \u2211h[i](1 - h[i+k}) ] * dx.  \n   - Representation: Use the same discretization as initial_h_values.  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n   a. Validate and preprocess initial_h_values if present. Check feasibility.  \n   b. Initialize GA population with initial_h_values scaled to meet constraints.  \n   c. Perform GA with custom mutation, crossover:  \n      - Mutation: Add Gaussian noise to selected individuals.  \n      - Crossover: Blend features from parents.  \n   d. Detect stagnation in GA (no improvement over iterations).  \n   e. Switch to Nelder-Mead:  \n      - Use best GA solution as initial simplex.  \n      - Optimize C\u2085 using simplex method.  \n      - Maintain feasibility constraints.  \n   f. Combine solutions: Track best from both methods.  \n\n4. Search choices and variations  \n   - Population size: 50. Mutation rate: 0.2. Stagnation threshold: 30.  \n   - Mutation operator: Gaussian with adaptive variance.  \n   - Crossover: Blend \u03b1=0.5.  \n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n   - Time budget: 1100s. Use both methods within budget.  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n   - Ensure 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and \u2211h = n_points/2.  \n   - Compute C\u2085 using evaluator after optimization.",
